{"id":"ff820d88f79bf52c","group":"58","path":"58/batch20/58-thm-tarski-vaught.md","title":"Tarski Vaught","display":"thm-tarski-vaught — Tarski Vaught","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-tarski-vaught","aliases":["58-thm-tarski-vaught"],"display":"thm-tarski-vaught — Tarski Vaught","depends_on":["[[58-df-elementary-substructure]]","[[58-df-elementary]]","[[58-df-formula]]","[[58-df-satisfaction]]","[[58-df-assignment]]","[[58-df-substructure]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-tarski-vaught"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-tarski-vaught</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-tarski-vaught — Tarski Vaught"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"faf104362ffe13b3\" href=\"?note=faf104362ffe13b3\" title=\"58-df-elementary-substructure\">58-df-elementary-substructure</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"e91c1261e1c2374b\" href=\"?note=e91c1261e1c2374b\" title=\"58-df-elementary\">58-df-elementary</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"65418b505fc53093\" href=\"?note=65418b505fc53093\" title=\"58-df-formula\">58-df-formula</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"8b6a90316aad78a4\" href=\"?note=8b6a90316aad78a4\" title=\"58-df-satisfaction\">58-df-satisfaction</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"64f35ba2e87964e0\" href=\"?note=64f35ba2e87964e0\" title=\"58-df-assignment\">58-df-assignment</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"563f382027630287\" href=\"?note=563f382027630287\" title=\"58-df-substructure\">58-df-substructure</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L,\\mathcal N,\\mathcal M\\in V\">\\(L,\\mathcal N,\\mathcal M\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Substructure}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Substructure}_S\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Fml}_S(L)\">\\(\\mathrm{Fml}_S(L)\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Var}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Var}_S\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Univ}\">\\(\\mathrm{Univ}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Assign}\">\\(\\mathrm{Assign}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Satisfaction}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Satisfaction}_S\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\prec_L\">\\(\\prec_L\\)</span> are the exact source symbols</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"s[x\\mapsto a]\">\\(s[x\\mapsto a]\\)</span> is the registered assignment update</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{TarskiVaughtCriterion}_S(\\mathcal N,\\mathcal M,L)\">\\(\\mathrm{TarskiVaughtCriterion}_S(\\mathcal N,\\mathcal M,L)\\)</span> (predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}tarski\\text{-}vaught\\text{-}criterion}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{TarskiVaughtCriterion}_S(\\mathcal N,\\mathcal M,L)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{Substructure}_S(\\mathcal N,\\mathcal M,L)\n\\land\\exists\\operatorname{Val}_{\\mathcal M},\\operatorname{Sat}_{\\mathcal M}\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Satisfaction}_S(\\mathcal M,L,\\operatorname{Val}_{\\mathcal M},\\operatorname{Sat}_{\\mathcal M})\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\forall x\\in\\mathrm{Var}_S\\;\\forall\\varphi\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(L)\\;\\forall s\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Assign}(\\mathcal N,s)\\land\\mathrm{Assign}(\\mathcal M,s)\n\\land\\operatorname{Sat}_{\\mathcal M}(\\exists x\\,\\varphi,s)\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{53mm}\\to\\exists a\\in\\mathrm{Univ}(\\mathcal N)\\;\n\\operatorname{Sat}_{\\mathcal M}(\\varphi,s[x\\mapsto a])\n\\Bigr)\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}tarski\\text{-}vaught\\text{-}criterion}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{TarskiVaughtCriterion}_S(\\mathcal N,\\mathcal M,L)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{Substructure}_S(\\mathcal N,\\mathcal M,L)\n\\land\\exists\\operatorname{Val}_{\\mathcal M},\\operatorname{Sat}_{\\mathcal M}\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Satisfaction}_S(\\mathcal M,L,\\operatorname{Val}_{\\mathcal M},\\operatorname{Sat}_{\\mathcal M})\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\forall x\\in\\mathrm{Var}_S\\;\\forall\\varphi\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(L)\\;\\forall s\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Assign}(\\mathcal N,s)\\land\\mathrm{Assign}(\\mathcal M,s)\n\\land\\operatorname{Sat}_{\\mathcal M}(\\exists x\\,\\varphi,s)\\\\\n&amp;\\hspace{53mm}\\to\\exists a\\in\\mathrm{Univ}(\\mathcal N)\\;\n\\operatorname{Sat}_{\\mathcal M}(\\varphi,s[x\\mapsto a])\n\\Bigr)\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}tarski\\text{-}vaught}\\vdash\n\\mathcal N\\prec_L\\mathcal M\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{TarskiVaughtCriterion}_S(\\mathcal N,\\mathcal M,L).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}tarski\\text{-}vaught}\\vdash\n\\mathcal N\\prec_L\\mathcal M\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{TarskiVaughtCriterion}_S(\\mathcal N,\\mathcal M,L).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The test reduces elementarity to witnesses for existential formulas, but now uses one selected satisfaction recursion and actual assignment updates rather than applying <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\models\">\\(\\models\\)</span> to an unencoded parameter tuple.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-elementary-substructure","status":"resolved","id":"faf104362ffe13b3","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-elementary-substructure]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-elementary","status":"resolved","id":"e91c1261e1c2374b","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-elementary]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-formula","status":"resolved","id":"65418b505fc53093","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-formula]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-satisfaction","status":"resolved","id":"8b6a90316aad78a4","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-satisfaction]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-assignment","status":"resolved","id":"64f35ba2e87964e0","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-assignment]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-substructure","status":"resolved","id":"563f382027630287","anchor":"ref-6","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-substructure]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"L,\\mathcal N,\\mathcal M\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Substructure}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Fml}_S(L)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Var}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Univ}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Assign}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Satisfaction}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\prec_L","display":false},{"tex":"s[x\\mapsto a]","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{TarskiVaughtCriterion}_S(\\mathcal N,\\mathcal M,L)","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n&\\mathrm{df\\text{-}tarski\\text{-}vaught\